        allocution: "\"I thought it was still open. I'll stay off.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} signed for the certified letter.", "The letter was addressed to a similar name at a different address, signed by a stranger."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you see the sign?", "\"Not until I was past it. I came up from the field edge, and I was already dragging the kayak.\""), .direct("Did you get the letter?", "\"No. I did not receive any certified letter, and I did not sign for one.\""), .direct("Why did you cross that field?", "\"Everyone launches there. Locals have used that landing for generations, and I learned it from my relatives.\""), .direct("How did you get to the creek?", "\"I dragged the kayak across the field. I did not see another way that morning, and I did not think anyone minded.\""), .direct("What would you have done if you saw the sign?", "\"I would have turned around. I do not want to trespass, and I would have used the downstream landing.\""), .direct("What do you want the owner to know?", "\"I am so sorry. I did not know it was closed, and I will never cross that field again.\""), .cross("A posted sign hung at the gate, didn't it?", "\"I saw one after I was past it. I did not see it coming in.\""), .cross("The owner mailed a certified letter, didn't {V.he}?", "\"So I hear. I never received it, and I do not know who did.\""), .cross("You dragged a kayak through a posted field, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did, and I know the trail camera shows it. I wish I had seen the sign.\""), .cross("You knew about the dispute over the landing, didn't you?", "\"I knew some people were unhappy. I did not know it was closed.\""), .cross("The downstream access is two miles away, isn't it?", "\"Yes. It is farther, and I chose the closer way. I should have checked.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} posted a gate and mailed a certified letter after paddlers began crossing a field to reach a creek. A trail camera filmed {D} dragging a kayak past a posted sign at 7:40 a.m.", "Locals have used that landing for generations, and {D} never got the letter and never saw the sign until past it. An honest mistake on an old path is not a crime."),
        closings: ("A sign at the gate, a certified letter, and a camera that shows {D} dragging a kayak right past. The notice was posted, and {D} crossed anyway.", "A landing used for generations, a letter {D} never received, and a sign seen too late. The State must prove {D} knew the field was closed."),
        timeline: [(-60, "The certified letter is mailed."), (0, "7:40 a.m.: {DL} drags the kayak."), (0, "9 a.m.: {V} checks the camera.")],
        identified: "A trail camera.",
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "mistakeOfFact"])

    static let loyaltyCardClonesV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.loyaltyCardClones",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Restaurant Server Photographed Cards at Tables, Bank Says", "Fifty-Eight Cards Share One Dinner Spot"],
        law: "cardFraud",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Used a device to copy and reuse card data of {V} and others, totaling $11,200, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A bank traced 58 compromised cards to one restaurant on {DATE}. A server, {D}, was filmed holding cards below the table for twenty seconds. Photos of card faces were on {D}'s phone. {DL} says {D.he} photographed cards to split checks.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Bank Analysis", "58 cards share the same restaurant, with $11,200 in fraud."), E(.digital, 3, "Phone Photos", "41 photos of card fronts and backs.", .search), E(.video, 2, "Restaurant Camera", "{D} holds a card below the table for twenty seconds.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Split Checks", "{DL} says {D.he} photographed cards to split checks.")],
        role: "Bank fraud investigator",
        exam: [.direct("What did the bank find?", "\"58 compromised cards, all of which had been used at the same restaurant. The fraud total was $11,200 across those accounts.\""), .direct("How did you narrow it to one restaurant?", "\"By mapping every card's recent purchases. The restaurant was the one location every compromised card had in common.\""), .direct("What did the restaurant camera show?", "\"{D}, a server, holding a customer's card below the table for about twenty seconds, out of sight of the diners.\""), .direct("What was found on {D}'s phone?", "\"41 photos of card fronts and backs. Many show the number, the expiration date, and the security code clearly.\""), .direct("How many servers work at that restaurant?", "\"Eleven. Several others handle cards too, so we looked at each of them.\""), .direct("How was the fraud carried out?", "\"Cloned cards and online purchases using the stolen numbers. The charges hit over about a month.\""), .cross("Did {D} use any of the numbers?", "\"We do not know. We found no purchase that we could connect to {D} personally.\""), .cross("Do servers need to handle cards?", "\"Yes. At every restaurant, servers take cards to the machine and bring them back. It is the job.\""), .cross("Is holding a card below a table suspicious by itself?", "\"It can be. Some servers do it out of habit, and the camera alone does not prove a copy was made.\""), .cross("Did you check the other ten servers' phones?", "\"We checked those we could reach. We found nothing as clear as {D}'s photos, but we did not get every phone.\""), .cross("Did {D} cooperate?", "\"Yes. {D} handed over the phone and explained the photos right away.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Server",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What do you do at the restaurant?", "\"I am a server. I have worked there a couple of years, handling tables, orders, and payments.\""), .direct("Do servers split checks?", "\"Yes, all the time. Big parties want separate checks, and we have to work out who owes what.\""), .direct("Do servers photograph cards to split checks?", "\"No, we write them. I keep a pad and a pen, and I write down the last four digits.\""), .direct("How does the card machine work?", "\"It is at the front. We bring cards over, swipe them, and return them with the slip.\""), .direct("Have you seen {D} hold cards below the table?", "\"Yes. {D} has a habit of holding the cards low while sorting a stack. I have seen that for months.\""), .direct("How do other servers handle busy nights?", "\"Fast. We all work the same way, hurrying cards back and forth, and we do not always look at who is holding what.\""), .cross("Have you ever seen {D} photograph a card?", "\"I have not. I would not do it, and I do not know that {D} did.\""), .cross("Does the restaurant allow photographing cards?", "\"No. That is against policy. We are told never to take pictures of customers' cards.\""), .cross("Did you see {D}'s phone at work?", "\"Yes, on the counter and in an apron pocket. I did not look at what was on it.\""), .cross("Are you friendly with {D}?", "\"Yes. We have worked together a long time, but I would say the same if I did not like {D}.\""), .cross("Did you talk to the investigator?", "\"I did. I told the same story I am telling you.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} photographed cards to use them.", "Photos for split checks."),
        allocution: "\"I should have told the truth the first time.\"",
        truths: ("A chat group on {DL}'s phone lists card numbers by lot.", "Another server borrowed {DL}'s phone on a break and took the photos."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you copy cards?", "\"No. I never copied a card, never used a card number, and never sold one to anyone.\""), .direct("Why were there photos of cards on your phone?", "\"Splitting checks. A big table asks for separate checks, and I photographed cards to keep track of whose was whose.\""), .direct("Forty-one photos, why so many?", "\"It was a busy month, with many large parties and a lot of split checks. I forgot to delete them after each night.\""), .direct("Why did you hold a card below the table?", "\"Habit. I hold cards low while sorting a stack, so they do not drop on the floor.\""), .direct("Did you know photographing cards was against policy?", "\"I never considered the policy. I thought of it as a notebook, and I never showed anyone the pictures.\""), .direct("What do you want the jury to know?", "\"I made a mistake with my phone. I am not a thief, and I would never steal from a customer.\""), .cross("The photos show card numbers and security codes, don't they?", "\"Yes. They do. I took them to keep the numbers straight, and I never used them.\""), .cross("The camera shows you holding a card for twenty seconds, doesn't it?", "\"It does. I was sorting a stack at the time, and I was not copying anything.\""), .cross("You photographed 41 cards, didn't you?", "\"Yes, over about a month. I know it looks bad, and I understand why.\""), .cross("Fifty-eight cards were compromised at your restaurant, weren't they?", "\"So the bank says. Eleven people handle cards there, and I am only one of them.\""), .cross("You were the only server with photos of card faces, weren't you?", "\"As far as I know. I cannot say what is on the other servers' phones.\"")],
        openings: ("A bank traced 58 compromised cards, $11,200 in fraud, to one restaurant. A server, {D}, was filmed holding a customer's card below the table for twenty seconds, and 41 photos of card fronts and backs were on {D}'s phone.", "{D} photographed cards to keep track of split checks and never used a number. Eleven servers handle cards at that restaurant, and a careless habit is not a scheme."),
        closings: ("Fifty-eight cards, one restaurant, twenty seconds below the table, and 41 photos on {D}'s phone. A server who photographs card faces has the means to steal.", "A busy month of split checks, a habit of holding cards low, and nothing showing {D} ever used a number. The State has photos and no theft."),
        timeline: [(-45, "The photos begin."), (-14, "Charges appear."), (0, "The bank flags the restaurant."), (3, "{DL} is questioned.")],
        identified: "A bank analysis.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let jailLockdownRiotV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.jailLockdownRiot",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Inmates Overturn Tables in Jail Cafeteria After Visits Canceled", "Cafeteria Brawl Injures Three Officers"],
        law: "riot",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Participated in a riot with three or more persons causing property damage and injury, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A cafeteria disturbance at a county jail on {DATE} began after visits were canceled. Tables flipped, trays flew, and three officers were hurt. {D} was filmed overturning a table. {DL} says {D.he} was shielding an older inmate.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Cafeteria Camera", "{D} overturns a table."), E(.statement, 3, "Officer", "'{D} shouted for the others to follow.'"), E(.forensic, 2, "Medical Reports", "Three officers hurt.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Shielding", "{DL} says {D.he} was shielding an older inmate.")],
        role: "Jail officer",
        exam: [.direct("What happened in the cafeteria that day?", "\"After visits were canceled, a disturbance broke out. Tables flipped, trays flew, and three officers were hurt in the crush.\""), .direct("What did {D} do?", "\"{D} overturned a table. I saw it from across the room, and the camera shows it as well.\""), .direct("Did {D} say anything?", "\"An officer reported that {D} shouted for the others to follow. I did not hear that myself over the noise.\""), .direct("How many inmates were in the room?", "\"Around forty. It was a meal period, and many were already upset about visits being canceled.\""), .direct("What injuries did the officers have?", "\"Three were hurt, with bruises, a sprain, and a cut to the head. All were treated and returned to duty in time.\""), .direct("How did you restore order?", "\"We called for backup, cleared the room, and locked down the unit. It took about fifteen minutes.\""), .cross("Did {D} hit anyone?", "\"Not that I saw. I did not see {D} strike an officer or another inmate.\""), .cross("Was {D} near an older inmate?", "\"Yes, briefly. {D} was beside an older inmate when the tables started to go.\""), .cross("Did you see who started the disturbance?", "\"No. It built quickly from several tables at once, and I could not say who started it.\""), .cross("Why were visits canceled?", "\"A staffing shortage and a lockdown on another unit. Inmates had been told the day before.\""), .cross("Were other inmates disciplined?", "\"Yes, a few. Several were written up for throwing trays.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Fellow inmate",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Where were you during the disturbance?", "\"In the cafeteria, at a table near the pillar. I am older, and I was eating slowly.\""), .direct("What did {D} do?", "\"{D} pulled me behind a pillar. I could not move fast, and tables were coming down all around us.\""), .direct("What did {D} do before that?", "\"Flipped a table. It all happened fast, and I saw it right before {D} grabbed my arm.\""), .direct("Why do you think {D} flipped the table?", "\"It looked like panic. A group rushed our side, and {D} shoved a table into the path.\""), .direct("Did {D} hit anyone?", "\"Not that I saw. {D} was busy keeping me out of the way.\""), .direct("Do you know {D}?", "\"From the unit. {D} is quiet and helps the older inmates with their trays and their legal papers.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} shout to the others?", "\"No. It was loud, and I could not hear anyone clearly.\""), .cross("Did you see who flipped the first table?", "\"I did not. I was looking at my food until the noise started.\""), .cross("Are you grateful to {D}?", "\"Yes. {D} may have kept me from being hurt, and I want to say so.\""), .cross("Did you feel anger about visits being canceled?", "\"Of course. Everyone did. We were told too late.\""), .cross("Did {D} tell you to follow along?", "\"No. {D} told me to get behind the pillar and stay down.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} helped lead a riot.", "Shielding someone."),
        allocution: "\"I regret it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} passed notes that morning urging a protest.", "{DL} pulled an officer out of the crush."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you lead the disturbance?", "\"No. I did not lead anything. I did not plan it and I did not tell anyone to join.\""), .direct("Why did you flip the table?", "\"Panic. People rushed toward our side, and I shoved a table to block them from reaching us.\""), .direct("Who were you with at that moment?", "\"An older inmate I help with trays. I pulled the older inmate behind a pillar to keep out of harm's way.\""), .direct("How did you feel about the canceled visits?", "\"Angry, like everybody. I was looking forward to seeing my family, and I was upset like the rest.\""), .direct("Did you strike anyone?", "\"No. I never hit an officer or another inmate. I only shoved the table and grabbed an arm.\""), .direct("What do you want the jury to know?", "\"I was trying to avoid trouble and protect someone. I did not want any of this to happen.\""), .cross("The camera shows you overturning a table, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. I did, and I regret it a lot. I did it in a panic and not to start trouble.\""), .cross("An officer says you shouted for the others to follow, doesn't the officer?", "\"That is what the officer says. I did not shout that, and I do not know where it came from.\""), .cross("Three officers were hurt, weren't they?", "\"I know. I am sorry for that. I was not involved in hurting anyone.\""), .cross("Visits were canceled and you were angry, weren't you?", "\"Yes, like many. Anger is not the same as leading a riot.\""), .cross("Throwing a table is violent, isn't it?", "\"It was a reaction to a crush of people. I should have found another way.\"")],
        openings: ("A cafeteria disturbance at a county jail began after visits were canceled. Tables flipped, trays flew, three officers were hurt, and a camera filmed {D} overturning a table while an officer says {D} shouted for others to follow.", "{D} flipped a table out of panic while shielding an older inmate. A frightened person in a crush is not a riot leader, and no one saw {D} hit anyone."),
        closings: ("Three officers hurt, a table overturned on camera, and a report of a shout to follow. {D} was at the center of it.", "Panic in a crowded room, an older inmate pulled behind a pillar, and no blow struck. The State must prove {D} led the riot and not that {D} reacted to it."),
        timeline: [(0, "11 a.m.: visits canceled."), (0, "12:15 p.m.: tables flip."), (0, "12:30 p.m.: injuries."), (0, "1 p.m.: order restored.")],
        identified: "A cafeteria camera.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let lakeCrashFatalV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.lakeCrashFatal",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Truck Crosses Causeway Median, Passenger Killed", "Sleep Aid and a Long Drive"],
        law: "invManslaughter",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Unlawfully killed {V} without malice by a culpably negligent act, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 21...55,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A truck crossed the median of a lake causeway at 1:20 a.m. on {DATE} and rolled. {V}, a passenger, died. {D}, the driver, had taken a prescription sleep aid and had a 0.04 reading. {DL} says a medical episode caused the crash.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Toxicology", "A sleep aid in {D}'s blood and a 0.04."), E(.document, 3, "Crash Report", "No braking; 58 in a 45."), E(.document, 2, "Prescription Label", "'Do not drive after taking.'")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Medical Episode", "{DL} says {D.he} blacked out.")],
        role: "State Highway Patrol trooper",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find at the scene?", "\"A truck rolled over after crossing the median of a lake causeway at 1:20 a.m. {V}, the passenger, had died.\""), .direct("What was the truck's speed?", "\"58 miles an hour in a 45 zone, based on the crash data and the scene reconstruction.\""), .direct("Was there any braking before the crossing?", "\"None. There were no skid marks and no sign the driver tried to slow before the truck crossed the median.\""), .direct("What did the toxicology show?", "\"A prescription sleep aid in {D}'s blood, and a 0.04 alcohol reading. That is under the legal limit but not zero.\""), .direct("What did the prescription label say?", "\"'Do not drive after taking.' It was in the truck, on the bottle, and printed in plain type.\""), .direct("What was the condition of the road?", "\"Dry and in good order. I found no pothole, no debris, and nothing that would explain the move across the median.\""), .cross("Could a blackout explain no braking?", "\"I cannot say. A person who blacks out would not brake, but I cannot tell you that is what happened.\""), .cross("Any fault in the road or the truck?", "\"No. I did not find a road fault. The truck's mechanics looked normal after the crash.\""), .cross("Was {D} impaired by alcohol?", "\"A 0.04 is below the legal limit. I cannot say it caused anything on its own.\""), .cross("Did {D} cooperate?", "\"Yes. {D} stayed at the scene, was devastated, and answered what questions {D} could.\""), .cross("Did {D} tell you about the pill?", "\"Yes. {D} said it was taken hours before and that the last memory was before the bridge.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Doctor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your field?", "\"I am a doctor, an internist. I diagnose and treat a wide range of conditions, including neurologic ones.\""), .direct("Could a seizure explain this crash?", "\"Yes, it could. A seizure can cause a sudden loss of control, with no braking and no steering correction.\""), .direct("What signs would fit a seizure?", "\"A truck that drifts and does not react, a driver who remembers nothing, and no sign of evasive action.\""), .direct("Was a seizure diagnosed in {D} before?", "\"No. {D} had no prior diagnosis, so no one had warned {D} to avoid driving.\""), .direct("Could a sleep aid cause a seizure?", "\"Rarely. A sleep aid can lower the seizure threshold in some people, though it is not common.\""), .direct("What would you want to know to settle it?", "\"An exam and tests, such as a scan and an EEG. Without them, I cannot say what happened.\""), .cross("Could the sleep aid alone explain the crash?", "\"Yes, it could. A person who takes a sleep aid and drives can fall asleep at the wheel.\""), .cross("Did you examine {D} before the crash?", "\"No. I reviewed records after the crash, and I did not see {D} as a patient.\""), .cross("Is a seizure the only explanation for no braking?", "\"No. Falling asleep fits equally well. I cannot choose between them without more information.\""), .cross("Did the label warn about driving?", "\"Yes. It said not to drive after taking it. That is a clear warning.\""), .cross("Would a person with a seizure know in advance?", "\"Often not, when it is a first seizure. That is why I say a prior diagnosis matters.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drove drowsy and impaired and killed a passenger.", "A medical episode."),
        allocution: "\"I'll live with it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} texted a coworker, 'about to take my pill, long drive anyway.'", "A scan later found a seizure condition {DL} had not been told about."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take the pill?", "\"Hours before. I took it in the evening, and I did not feel drowsy when I left.\""), .direct("What do you remember of the drive?", "\"Nothing after the bridge. I remember the road and the lights, and then I woke up after the crash.\""), .direct("Did you read the label?", "\"I read it. It said not to drive after taking it, and I thought enough hours had passed.\""), .direct("Had you been drinking?", "\"One beer. I did not feel it, and I did not think it mattered.\""), .direct("How did {V} come to be in the truck?", "\"{V} asked for a ride, and I said yes. We were friends, and I trusted myself to drive.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"I am devastated. {V} trusted me, and I will carry this for the rest of my life.\""), .cross("You took a pill that said not to drive after taking, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I should have waited longer or found another ride. I regret it deeply.\""), .cross("You had a beer on top of the pill, didn't you?", "\"One beer, hours earlier. I know that was not wise.\""), .cross("You were doing 58 in a 45, weren't you?", "\"That is what the report says. I do not remember my speed.\""), .cross("You never braked, did you?", "\"I do not remember. Something happened to me on that bridge, and I do not know what.\""), .cross("You chose to drive, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did, and I take that responsibility.\"")],
        openings: ("A truck crossed the median of a lake causeway at 1:20 a.m. and rolled, killing {V}, a passenger. {D}, the driver, had a prescription sleep aid in {D}'s blood, a 0.04 reading, and no braking before the crash.", "{D} remembers nothing after the bridge, and a medical episode can strike with no warning. A tragic crash is not a crime unless the State proves {D} was reckless."),
        closings: ("58 in a 45, no braking, a sleep aid labeled not to drive, and a 0.04. {D} knew the warning and drove anyway.", "No fault in the road, no prior diagnosis, and a driver who remembers nothing. A medical emergency is a tragedy, and the State has not ruled it out."),
        timeline: [(0, "9 p.m.: {D} takes the pill."), (0, "1 a.m.: {D} drives onto the causeway."), (0, "1:20 a.m.: the truck crosses the median."), (0, "3 a.m.: blood is drawn.")],
        identified: "A trooper's report and toxicology.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant was impaired at the time of the offense"],
        mood: .divided,
        impact: "{V} was the best part of my family.")

    static let pillPressV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.pillPress",
        category: .drugs,
        headlines: ["Barn Fire Exposes Pill Press and Powder", "Firefighters Find Blue Pills Stamped 'M 30'"],
        law: "traffickingOpioid28",
        threshold: 11,
        spec: "Trafficked in opioids by manufacturing and possessing 28 grams or more of a mixture containing fentanyl, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 24...40,
        victim: false,
        summary: "Firefighters put out a barn fire on {DATE} and found a pill press, dye, and bags of blue pills stamped 'M 30' weighing 520 grams. A lab found fentanyl. The barn was leased to {D}. {DL} says a subtenant used it.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Press and Pills", "A press, dye, and 520 grams of blue pills in the barn.", .search), E(.forensic, 3, "Lab Report", "Fentanyl in the pills."), E(.document, 3, "Hardware Receipts", "Dye and binder bought on {D}'s card."), E(.document, 2, "Lease", "The barn leased to {D}.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Subtenant", "{DL} says a subtenant used the barn.")],
        role: "Fire marshal",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find after the barn fire?", "\"A pill press, dye, and bags of blue pills stamped 'M 30', weighing 520 grams in total.\""), .direct("What did the lab find in the pills?", "\"Fentanyl. The pills were counterfeit versions of a prescription tablet, and each one carried a dangerous amount.\""), .direct("Who leased the barn?", "\"{D}. The lease is in {D}'s name, and the rent was paid to the landowner each month.\""), .direct("How was the barn secured?", "\"With a padlock on the door. The padlock survived the fire, and a key was not found in the barn.\""), .direct("What did the hardware receipts show?", "\"Dye and binder bought on {D}'s card. Those are materials used to make pills look like real tablets.\""), .direct("What did you get from the press?", "\"We looked for prints and found none. The fire burned the surfaces, and heat destroys most prints.\""), .cross("Were fingerprints found?", "\"No. They were burned. We have no print from {D} or anyone else on the press.\""), .cross("Who else had access to the barn?", "\"I cannot say. A padlock keeps people out, but anyone with a key or a pair of bolt cutters could get in.\""), .cross("Does a lease prove who used the barn?", "\"No. A lease proves who rented it. It does not tell you who ran a press inside.\""), .cross("How did the fire start?", "\"We never found the cause. It may have started near the press, but I cannot rule out other sources.\""), .cross("Did {D} cooperate?", "\"{D} spoke with us. {D} said a subtenant used the barn and gave us a first name.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Neighbor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"I live on the next property. I see the barn from my back porch, and I have known {D} a couple of years.\""), .direct("Who was at the barn?", "\"A driver in a white van, at night. I saw the van come and go on several nights.\""), .direct("Did you see {D} there?", "\"Sometimes, in the day. {D} would stop by to check on the place and sometimes mow around it.\""), .direct("What did you notice at night?", "\"Lights in the barn late, a van parked behind it, and a chemical smell once that I could not place.\""), .direct("Did you ever speak to the person in the van?", "\"No. I kept my distance. The person did not seem friendly, and I did not want trouble.\""), .direct("Did you tell anyone?", "\"I mentioned it to {D}, who said a subtenant was using the barn for storage.\""), .cross("Did you ever see {D} at night at the barn?", "\"Not that I recall. Most of what I saw at night was the van.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} carry anything in or out?", "\"Mowing equipment and a few boxes, in the day. I did not know what was in them.\""), .cross("Could you see the van's plate?", "\"No. I never got close enough, and it was dark.\""), .cross("Did you call the sheriff about the van?", "\"No. I did not. I assumed it was someone {D} knew.\""), .cross("Are you friends with {D}?", "\"We are neighbors. We help each other with fences and trash.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} ran a pill press in a leased barn.", "A subtenant."),
        allocution: "\"I knew he used it. I did not know for what.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s phone has a photo of a tray of pills captioned 'barn batch.'", "The subtenant was later arrested in Tennessee with a second press."),
        defendant: [.direct("Was it your barn?", "\"On paper. I signed the lease, but I did not use it for much myself.\""), .direct("Who used the barn?", "\"A subtenant. The subtenant paid cash, and I took it each month without asking questions.\""), .direct("What do you know about the subtenant?", "\"A first name and a phone number that no longer works. I never saw the inside of the barn when it was in use.\""), .direct("Your card bought the dye?", "\"The subtenant borrowed it. I let the subtenant use my card for supplies, because that is what the subtenant said was needed.\""), .direct("Did you know about fentanyl?", "\"I never knew. If I had known, I would have called the sheriff the same day.\""), .direct("What do you want the jury to know?", "\"I made a poor choice to trust a stranger. I did not run a drug operation.\""), .cross("You leased the barn, and your card bought the dye, didn't it?", "\"Yes, my card, borrowed. I know that looks bad, and I should not have lent it.\""), .cross("You took cash from the subtenant each month, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It was rent, and I did not ask what the barn was used for.\""), .cross("The press and 520 grams of pills were in your barn, weren't they?", "\"Yes, in a barn I leased. I did not know what was in there.\""), .cross("You never visited the inside of the barn while it was in use?", "\"No. I checked outside and stayed out. I did not want to disturb the subtenant.\""), .cross("Can you produce the subtenant?", "\"No. The subtenant disappeared after the fire. I told investigators everything I knew.\"")],
        openings: ("Firefighters put out a barn fire and found a pill press, dye, and 520 grams of blue 'M 30' pills that tested positive for fentanyl. The barn was leased to {D}, and the dye and binder were bought on {D}'s card.", "A subtenant paid {D} cash to use the barn, borrowed {D}'s card, and vanished after the fire. A landlord who stayed out of the barn did not run a pill press."),
        closings: ("A lease in {D}'s name, dye bought on {D}'s card, and a press with 520 grams of fentanyl pills. The barn was {D}'s, and so is the responsibility.", "A rented barn, a borrowed card, burned prints, and a subtenant no one can find. The State has paper trails, but no one who saw {D} press a pill."),
        timeline: [(-30, "{DL} subleases the barn."), (-3, "Dye is purchased."), (0, "2 a.m.: the barn burns."), (45, "The lab confirms fentanyl.")],
        identified: "A barn fire.",
        aggravating: ["The offense endangered public safety"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["searchSeizure", "burdenOfProof"])

    static let clerkShootsBackV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.clerkShootsBack",
        category: .robbery,
        headlines: ["Gas Station Clerk Fires on Masked Robber, Who Escapes", "Partial Plate and a Graze Lead to Arrest"],
        law: "dangerousRobbery",
        threshold: 10,
        spec: "Took $540 from the person and presence of {V}, a gas station clerk, by the use of a handgun, whereby {V.his} life was threatened, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...27,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Two masked people robbed a gas station clerk, {V}, at gunpoint at about 10:40 p.m. on {DATE}. {V} fired once as they ran. An ATM camera caught a partial plate. Twenty minutes later {D} sought urgent care for an arm graze. {DL} says {D.he} fell on a fence.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Store Camera", "Two masked people; one pointing a handgun.", .search), E(.video, 3, "ATM Camera", "A car with a partial plate leaves the lot."), E(.document, 2, "Urgent Care Record", "{D} treated for a graze, 20 minutes after, ten blocks away."), E(.statement, 2, "Cousin", "A cousin says {D} borrowed the car that night.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Fence", "{DL} says {D.he} fell on a fence.")],
        role: "Gas station clerk",
        exam: [.direct("What happened that night?", "\"Two masked people came in at about 10:40 and pointed a pistol at me. I was alone at the counter and gave them what was in the drawer.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I fired once as they ran out. I had a handgun under the counter, and I fired toward the door.\""), .direct("Could you see their faces?", "\"No. Both wore masks. I saw heights and clothing, and I could not tell you anything about their faces.\""), .direct("What did the store camera show?", "\"Two masked people, and one of them pointing a handgun at me. It also shows me firing as they leave.\""), .direct("What happened to the car?", "\"An ATM camera in the lot caught a car with a partial plate leaving. Deputies ran the partial from there.\""), .direct("How did you feel afterward?", "\"Shaking, scared, and sick. I had never fired a gun at a person, and I did not know whether I had hit anyone.\""), .cross("Did you hit anyone?", "\"I am not sure. I fired once as they ran, and I did not see anyone fall.\""), .cross("Could you tell the height or build of the one with the gun?", "\"Average height, thin. I cannot say more, and I would not swear it was {D}.\""), .cross("Did you recognize a voice?", "\"They said very little. I would not recognize a voice from that.\""), .cross("How far was the door when you fired?", "\"About twenty feet. They were already running, and I fired quickly.\""), .cross("Did you know {D} before that night?", "\"No. I had never seen {D}, and I cannot place {D} at my store.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Neighbor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Where do you live in relation to the fence?", "\"Across the street. I can see the fence from my front window and walk by it most days.\""), .direct("What is the fence like?", "\"Chain link with a broken top. The wire sticks up in a few places, and it catches people who climb over.\""), .direct("Do people cut across there?", "\"Yes, often. Kids and neighbors climb it to shortcut to the store, and I see scrapes on their arms.\""), .direct("Have you seen anyone hurt on it?", "\"Yes. A kid last summer ripped a sleeve and scraped an arm. It is sharp on top.\""), .direct("Did you see {D} that night?", "\"Not that night. I know {D} lives around here and uses that shortcut.\""), .direct("Does the fence get fixed?", "\"No. I have complained to the property owner for years, and nothing is done.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} fall on the fence?", "\"No. I did not see anyone fall that night.\""), .cross("What time did you look out the window?", "\"I do not remember. I was home, but I was not watching the fence.\""), .cross("Did you see anyone running that night?", "\"No. I heard a siren later, and I did not see what led to it.\""), .cross("Do you know where {D} was at 10:40?", "\"No. I do not, and I cannot say anything about that.\""), .cross("Are you friends with {D}?", "\"I know {D} from the block. I would say the same of any neighbor.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} and a partner robbed a clerk at gunpoint.", "A graze from a fence."),
        allocution: "\"I was hurt and scared. I am sorry for that clerk.\"",
        truths: ("The graze is shaped like a bullet path, not a fence cut.", "A second man arrested with the same partial tag confessed that {DL} was not there."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you rob the store?", "\"No. I did not rob anyone, and I did not point a gun at a clerk.\""), .direct("How did you get hurt?", "\"On a fence. I was climbing over a chain link fence near my place, and the top caught my arm.\""), .direct("Why did you go to urgent care?", "\"The cut was bleeding and it hurt. It was late, and urgent care was the only place open.\""), .direct("Whose car was the one on the ATM camera?", "\"My cousin's. I borrowed it that night and lent it out to someone else for a while.\""), .direct("Who did you lend it to?", "\"A friend I will name for investigators. I did not know what the friend planned to do with the car.\""), .direct("What do you want the jury to know?", "\"I was hurt on a fence, got treated, and went home. I had nothing to do with that robbery.\""), .cross("You went to urgent care twenty minutes after the robbery, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It is a coincidence. I was hurt on the fence, and I went when the bleeding got bad.\""), .cross("Urgent care was ten blocks away, wasn't it?", "\"About that. It is the closest one to where I live.\""), .cross("You had borrowed the car that night, hadn't you?", "\"Yes, from my cousin. I lent it out, and I did not drive it at that hour.\""), .cross("The clerk fired once and may have hit someone, didn't the clerk?", "\"I know that. I was not at the store, and the cut on my arm came from the fence.\""), .cross("You cannot prove how you got that cut, can you?", "\"The fence is there, and a neighbor knows how sharp it is. I did not get it from a bullet.\"")],
        openings: ("Two masked people robbed a gas station clerk at gunpoint, and {V} fired once as they ran. An ATM camera caught a partial plate, and twenty minutes later, ten blocks away, {D} sought urgent care for a graze on the arm.", "{D} cut an arm on a broken chain link fence and went to urgent care when it kept bleeding. A coincidence of time and place is not a robbery."),
        closings: ("A masked robbery, a shot fired at the door, a car with a partial plate, and {D} at urgent care twenty minutes later with a graze. The timing is too neat to ignore.", "A broken fence that cuts neighbors every year, a borrowed car lent out, and a clerk who never saw a face. The State cannot show {D} held that gun."),
        timeline: [(0, "10:40 p.m.: the robbery."), (0, "10:41 p.m.: {V} fires."), (0, "11 p.m.: {D} at urgent care."), (6, "{D} charged.")],
        identified: "An ATM camera and an urgent care record.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "I quit that job.",
        doctrines: ["accompliceTestimony", "burdenOfProof"])

    static let toddlerFentanylV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.toddlerFentanyl",
        category: .family,
        headlines: ["Toddler Unresponsive After Chewing Powder From Coat Pocket", "Baggie in a Jacket Within a Child's Reach"],
        law: "childAbuseMisd",
        threshold: 9,
        spec: "Being the parent of a two-year-old child, created a substantial risk of physical injury to the child other than by accidental means, by leaving fentanyl within the child's reach, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 21...35,
        victim: false,
        summary: "On {DATE}, {D} called 911 after {D.his} two-year-old was found limp. Paramedics gave naloxone and the child recovered after two days in the hospital. Deputies found a baggie of fentanyl powder in a coat hanging on a hook at toddler height. {DL} says the coat belonged to a visiting friend.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Hospital Records", "Opioid toxicity, naloxone given, two days in the pediatric unit."), E(.physical, 3, "Baggie in Coat", "A baggie of fentanyl powder in a coat on a low hook.", .search), E(.digital, 3, "Texts", "{DL}'s message the day before: 'got a gram, need any?'", .search)],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Visiting Friend", "A friend left a coat at the apartment that week."), E(.statement, 1, "Fast Call", "{DL} called 911 immediately.")],
        role: "Emergency doctor",
        exam: [.direct("How sick was the child when you saw the child?", "\"Barely breathing, with tiny pupils and slow responses. The child was in serious danger when brought in.\""), .direct("What did the tests show?", "\"Fentanyl in the child's blood. It was an opioid toxicity, and that was the cause of the breathing trouble.\""), .direct("What treatment did the child receive?", "\"Naloxone from the paramedics, then supportive care in our unit. The child spent two days in the pediatric unit.\""), .direct("Did the fast 911 call help?", "\"Very much. Minutes matter with opioids in a child, and the caller got paramedics there quickly.\""), .direct("Did the child recover?", "\"Yes. After two days the breathing stabilized, and the child went home with follow-up care.\""), .direct("How does a two-year-old come into contact with fentanyl?", "\"Usually by swallowing or touching powder left within reach. A tiny amount can be dangerous for a child that small.\""), .cross("Can you say whose powder it was?", "\"No. Testing tells me what substance, not whose it was or how it got to the child.\""), .cross("Did {D} show concern at the hospital?", "\"Yes. {D} stayed at the bedside, answered every question, and appeared frightened.\""), .cross("Did {D} call right away?", "\"The records show the 911 call came quickly after the child was found limp.\""), .cross("Could someone other than {D} have left the powder?", "\"I cannot say. That is for investigators, and I treat children.\""), .cross("Did the child have a history of problems?", "\"No. The child was healthy before this.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Visitor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you leave a coat at {D}'s home?", "\"Yes, that week. I visited, hung the coat on a hook by the door, and forgot it when I left.\""), .direct("Was the coat yours?", "\"The coat, yes. The baggie, no. I never put a baggie in that coat.\""), .direct("What else was in the pockets?", "\"Gloves, a receipt, and some loose change. That is what I remember.\""), .direct("Did you know there was fentanyl near the child?", "\"No. I had no idea, and I am horrified that the child was hurt.\""), .direct("How long were you at the home?", "\"An afternoon. We had lunch, talked, and I left the coat on the hook when I went.\""), .direct("Do you use drugs?", "\"I will not discuss that here. I can tell you I would never leave anything near a child.\""), .cross("You deny the baggie was yours, don't you?", "\"Yes. It was not mine, and I do not know how it ended up in my coat.\""), .cross("Who had access to the coat after you left?", "\"Anyone in the house. It hung on a hook within reach of the child.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} touch the coat?", "\"No. I was not there after I left, so I cannot say.\""), .cross("Did you talk to {D} after the hospital?", "\"Briefly. We were both shaken, and neither of us understood what happened.\""), .cross("Do you want to protect {D}?", "\"I want the truth. I am here because I left a coat, and I apologize.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} left fentanyl where a toddler could reach it.", "A visitor's coat."),
        allocution: "\"I'm in treatment now. I almost lost my child.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s own hair test came back positive for fentanyl.", "The visitor's fingerprints, not {DL}'s, were on the baggie."),
        defendant: [.direct("Whose powder was it?", "\"Not mine. I never owned, used, or sold fentanyl, and I did not know it was in the house.\""), .direct("What happened that afternoon?", "\"I found my child limp and called 911 right away. I started to panic, and I kept the line open until help came.\""), .direct("What about the text from the day before?", "\"I sent it to a friend as talk. I did not have a gram, and I never bought anything.\""), .direct("A coat hung on a hook at toddler height, didn't it?", "\"It did, a visitor's coat. I did not check the pockets, and I wish I had.\""), .direct("What did you do when paramedics arrived?", "\"I told them what I knew and rode with my child to the hospital. I did not leave the bedside.\""), .direct("How are you coping with what happened?", "\"Sick. I will never forgive myself for not checking that coat, and I am grateful the child is alive.\""), .cross("The text said 'got a gram, need any?' didn't it?", "\"That is the text. It was talk, and it was a poor way to joke.\""), .cross("A baggie of fentanyl powder was in a coat in your home, wasn't it?", "\"In a visitor's coat, yes. I did not know it was there.\""), .cross("You did not check the pockets of a coat hanging at your child's height, did you?", "\"No. I did not. That is my failing.\""), .cross("You are saying a visitor left fentanyl in your home, aren't you?", "\"I am saying it was not mine. I do not know who put it there.\""), .cross("Your child nearly died in your home, didn't the child?", "\"Yes, and I called right away. That is what I did.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} called 911 after a two-year-old was found limp. Paramedics gave naloxone and the child recovered after two days in the hospital, and deputies found a baggie of fentanyl powder in a coat hanging at toddler height in {D}'s home.", "The coat belonged to a visiting friend, and the baggie was not {D}'s. {D} found the child limp and called right away, and a fast call is what saved a life."),
        closings: ("Fentanyl powder in a coat at a toddler's reach, a text offering a gram, and a child who nearly died. A home must be safe for a two-year-old, and this one was not.", "A visitor's coat, a baggie that was never {D}'s, and a call that saved a child's life. The State cannot show whose powder it was."),
        timeline: [(-1, "{DL} texts about a gram."), (-1, "A friend hangs a coat on the hook."), (0, "3:20 p.m.: the 911 call."), (2, "The child goes home.")],
        identified: "A hospital report and a search.",
        aggravating: ["The victim was very young"],
        mood: .divided)

    static let swattingCallV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.swattingCall",
        category: .cyber,
        headlines: ["False Report of Armed Man on Balcony Ends in Fatal Police Shooting", "Game Chat Feud Led to the Call"],
        law: "invManslaughter",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Unlawfully caused the death of {V} by making a false emergency report that led police to shoot {V.him} at {V.his} home, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 24...27,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, a caller reported a man with a rifle on an apartment balcony. Officers arrived and shot {V} when {V.he} stepped out holding a phone. The call used an internet phone account tied to {D}, who had threatened {V} in a game chat. {DL} says someone else used {D.his} account.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Call Records", "The call came from an internet phone account tied to {D}."), E(.digital, 3, "Game Chat", "{D} wrote that {V} would 'get a visit tonight.'"), E(.video, 2, "Body Camera", "{V} steps onto the balcony holding a phone.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Borrowed Account", "{DL} says others used {D.his} login.")],
        role: "Dispatch supervisor",
        exam: [.direct("What did the caller say?", "\"That someone with a rifle was standing on an apartment balcony. The caller sounded urgent and gave the address.\""), .direct("Where was the call traced?", "\"To an internet phone account tied to {D}. The account number and billing details point to {D}.\""), .direct("Was the voice recorded?", "\"Yes. It was a disguised voice, altered by software, so we could not identify the speaker.\""), .direct("Could another person use the account?", "\"With the password, yes. Anyone who knew the login could place a call through it.\""), .direct("What did the body camera show?", "\"{V} stepping onto the balcony holding a phone. Officers fired when {V} stepped out, and {V} died.\""), .direct("What was in the game chat?", "\"{D} wrote that {V} would 'get a visit tonight.' It was posted hours before the call.\""), .cross("Did {D} say anything about a rifle?", "\"Not in the chat I saw. The chat mentioned a visit, but I did not see a weapon mentioned.\""), .cross("Did you determine who held the account password?", "\"We learned others knew it. I do not have a complete list.\""), .cross("Was {D} at home when the call was made?", "\"We do not know. The call was routed over the internet, and the location was not reliable.\""), .cross("Could the disguised voice belong to anyone?", "\"Yes. It was altered. I cannot connect it to {D} or anyone else.\""), .cross("Did {D} cooperate with investigators?", "\"Yes. {D} met with us and answered questions without a lawyer at first.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} made a false call that got {V} killed.", "Someone borrowed {D}'s account."),
        allocution: "\"It was a stupid threat. I never thought it would happen.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s browser history includes a search for how to fake a caller ID.", "A third player in the chat admitted placing the call with {DL}'s login."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you make the call?", "\"No. I did not call 911, and I did not disguise my voice or report a rifle.\""), .direct("What was the threat in the chat?", "\"Trash talk. It was the kind of thing people say in a game, and I did not mean a real visit.\""), .direct("Whose account was it?", "\"Mine, but three friends had the password. We shared it for a gaming group and for cheap calls.\""), .direct("What did you mean by 'get a visit tonight'?", "\"Just words. I meant I would beat {V} in the next match and show up in the game.\""), .direct("How did you learn what happened?", "\"From investigators. I was shocked and sick. I had never imagined anything like that.\""), .direct("Looking back, how do you feel about {V}?", "\"I am heartbroken. {V} died because someone made a terrible call, and I wish I could take back my words.\""), .cross("The call came from your account, didn't it?", "\"It did. Others had the password, and I did not place it.\""), .cross("You wrote that {V} would get a visit tonight, didn't you?", "\"Yes, in a heated chat. I regret it deeply, and I never meant a real visit.\""), .cross("You had threatened {V} before, hadn't you?", "\"We traded insults. I did not threaten to hurt {V}.\""), .cross("You are the one with the account and the motive, aren't you?", "\"I am the one with the account. Others had the password, and I did not make the call.\""), .cross("Can you name who else had the password?", "\"Three friends. I gave their names to investigators.\"")],
        openings: ("A caller reported someone with a rifle on an apartment balcony. Officers shot {V} when {V.he} stepped out holding a phone, and the call came from an internet phone account tied to {D}, who had threatened {V} in a game chat.", "Three friends had the password to {D}'s internet phone account, and {D}'s game chat was trash talk. A disguised voice on a shared account proves no one in particular."),
        closings: ("A swatting call from {D}'s account, a chat promising {V} a visit, and an officer's shot at a balcony. {V} is dead because someone made that call.", "A shared password, a disguised voice, and an insult in a game chat. The State has not shown whose voice placed the call."),
        timeline: [(-3, "The game chat feud."), (0, "9:40 p.m.: the false call."), (0, "9:52 p.m.: officers arrive."), (0, "9:54 p.m.: the shooting.")],
        identified: "Call records.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "{V} only wanted to see what the noise was.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "expertTestimony"],
        genders: ["V": .male, "D": .male])

    static let scaffoldNoHarnessV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.scaffoldNoHarness",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Worker Buried in Unsupported Trench, Contractor Charged", "Shoring Box Sat Unused in the Yard"],
        law: "invManslaughter",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Unintentionally killed {V} without malice through culpable negligence, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V}, a laborer, died on {DATE} when a nine-foot trench wall collapsed. No shoring was in place. {D}, the contractor, had been warned about trench depth before. {DL} says the shoring box was delayed and {V} went in against instructions.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Inspection Warning", "A prior warning about trench depth on another job."), E(.forensic, 3, "Autopsy", "Asphyxia from a soil collapse."), E(.physical, 2, "Site Photos", "No shoring box; spoil pile at the edge.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Box Delayed", "{DL} says the shoring box was delayed and {V} went in anyway.")],
        role: "Safety inspector",
        exam: [.direct("Describe your work as a safety inspector.", "\"I inspect excavations and scaffolds for safety rules. I check depths, shoring, and ladders, and I write warnings when a contractor is not following the rules.\""), .direct("What did you find at the site on {DATE}?", "\"A nine-foot trench had collapsed. No shoring box was in place, and a spoil pile sat right at the edge of the trench.\""), .direct("How did {V} die?", "\"The autopsy found asphyxia from a soil collapse. {V} was buried when the trench wall gave way, and workers dug for over an hour to recover {V}.\""), .direct("What did the site photos show?", "\"No shoring box anywhere in the trench, and a spoil pile at the edge. Both are violations that make a collapse much more likely at that depth.\""), .direct("What had you told {D} about trench depth before?", "\"I issued a prior warning about trench depth on another job. {D} knew the rules, and that warning was in the file when this collapse happened.\""), .direct("What do the rules require at nine feet?", "\"Shoring, a box, or sloping so the walls cannot collapse. Nothing was in place, and workers should not enter a trench that deep without protection.\""), .cross("Did {D} say that a shoring box was ordered?", "\"Yes. {D} says the box was ordered and delayed. The supplier confirmed it was delivered the morning after the collapse.\""), .cross("Was there a shoring box at {D}'s yard?", "\"A box sat unused in {D}'s yard for about a week. I cannot say whether it was the right size for that trench.\""), .cross("Was {V} told to stay out of the trench?", "\"{D} says so. A crew member says {V} was told once. I cannot say how clear the instruction was or whether {V} heard it.\""), .cross("Was {V} the only person in the trench?", "\"Yes, as far as I know. No one else was in the trench when it collapsed, and the others on the crew were above ground.\""), .cross("Were you at the site on the morning of the collapse?", "\"No. I arrived after the collapse. I know what I saw in the photos and what crew members told me afterward.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Crew member",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Please describe your work on the crew.", "\"I am a crew member. I dig, set pipe, and backfill. I was working on the same job as {V} and {D} on the day of the collapse.\""), .direct("What did you hear {D} say about the trench?", "\"{D} told us to wait for the shoring box. {D} said it was on order and not to go in until it arrived.\""), .direct("Where was {D} when {V} went into the trench?", "\"{D} had stepped away to make a call. I saw {V} climb down with a shovel, and I did not think {V} would stay long.\""), .direct("What did the trench look like that morning?", "\"It was deep, with soft soil and a pile of dirt at the edge. I would not have gone in myself without a box.\""), .direct("What happened when the wall collapsed?", "\"It was fast. A wall of dirt fell all at once. We shouted for {D}, and everyone started digging by hand.\""), .direct("What did {D} do after the collapse?", "\"{D} ran back, called 911, and dug with us until help came. {D} was shaking and stayed until {V} was recovered.\""), .cross("Was {V} told to stay out of the trench?", "\"Yes. {D} told us all to wait. I heard it myself, but I did not stop {V} when I saw {V} going down.\""), .cross("Did {V} go in against instructions?", "\"Yes. {V} went in anyway. I think {V} wanted to get ahead on the work, and I did not say anything in time.\""), .cross("Was a box in the yard at the time?", "\"A smaller box sat in the yard. I do not think it fit this trench, but I did not measure it myself.\""), .cross("Did {D} check the trench before leaving the site?", "\"I do not remember. {D} left in a hurry for a call. I do not know whether {D} looked at the trench before leaving.\""), .cross("Did you tell anyone the trench was unsafe?", "\"No. I did not. I know I should have said something to {D} or to {V}, and I have thought about that every day.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sent a worker into an unsupported trench.", "A refusal to wait."),
        allocution: "\"I'll live with it.\"",
        truths: ("A shoring box sat unused in {DL}'s yard for a week.", "The supplier confirms the box was delivered the morning after."),
        defendant: [.direct("Please describe your company.", "\"I run a small excavation company. We dig trenches for water lines and drains, and I have worked in the trade for many years.\""), .direct("Did you order {V} to go into the trench?", "\"No. I did not. I told {V} to wait for the shoring box. I never wanted anyone in an unsupported trench.\""), .direct("What happened with the shoring box?", "\"I ordered one, and it was delayed. I had a smaller box in my yard, but it was not the right size for that depth.\""), .direct("Why did the work continue without the box?", "\"I thought the crew would wait. I left the site for a short time, and when I came back, {V} was already in the trench.\""), .direct("What did you do when the trench collapsed?", "\"I ran to help and called 911. We dug with shovels and our hands, and I will never forget how long it took.\""), .direct("How do you feel about what happened?", "\"The word for it is terrible. {V} died on my job, and I think about it every day. I should have taken the shovel from {V} myself.\""), .cross("You had been warned about trench depth before, hadn't you?", "\"Yes. I was warned once on another job. I understood the rule, and I know I should have been stricter on this one.\""), .cross("A shoring box sat unused in your yard for a week, didn't it?", "\"Yes. It was a smaller one. It was not right for this trench, and I did not try to use it, and that was my decision.\""), .cross("The spoil pile was at the edge of the trench, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It was close to the edge. That was a mistake, and it added weight to the wall that collapsed.\""), .cross("You were not on the site when {V} entered the trench, were you?", "\"I had stepped away for a short time. I know a contractor is supposed to be there, and I regret that I was not.\""), .cross("The box arrived the morning after the collapse, didn't it?", "\"Yes. It arrived the next morning. I know that is too late, and I wish it had come a day sooner.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}, a laborer, died on {DATE} when a nine-foot trench wall collapsed. No shoring was in place, a spoil pile sat at the edge, and {D}, the contractor, had been warned about trench depth before.", "The defense will present a contractor who told the crew to wait for a delayed shoring box, and a laborer who went into the trench anyway. A refusal to wait is not an order to enter."),
        closings: ("No shoring, nine feet down, a spoil pile at the edge, and a prior warning about trench depth. {V} died of asphyxia in a trench that a box would have protected, and the box sat unused in a yard.", "A delayed box, an instruction to wait, and a laborer who went in anyway. The State has not proved that {D} sent {V} into the trench, and the delivery date shows the delay was real."),
        timeline: [(-21, "The prior warning."), (-3, "The box is ordered."), (0, "9 a.m.: the collapse."), (0, "10:30 a.m.: {V} is recovered.")],
        identified: "An inspection warning.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "He had three kids.",
        doctrines: ["lesserIncluded"],
        genders: ["V": .male])

    static let outboardMotorsV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.outboardMotors",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Tree Service Trailer Stripped of Saws and Generator Overnight", "Yard Sale Ad Shows the Missing Saws"],
        law: "felonyLarceny",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Stole two chainsaws and a generator valued at $8,700 from {V}, a tree service, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 24...48,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, {V} found a locked trailer cut open and two chainsaws and a generator gone. Nine days later a yard-sale post from {D}'s account showed the saws. Serial numbers matched. {DL} says {D.he} bought them from a flea-market seller.",
        state: [E(.video, 2, "Trailer Camera", "A figure in a hood cuts the lock at 3:05 a.m."), E(.digital, 3, "Yard Sale Post", "{D} lists two saws 'barely used, $600 each.'"), E(.physical, 3, "Serial Numbers", "The saws match {V}'s records.", .search), E(.document, 2, "Value Records", "The saws and generator cost $8,700.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "Handwritten Receipt", "A scrap receipt: 'two saws, $1,200 cash.' No last name."), E(.statement, 1, "Past Dealings", "{DL} has resold used tools for years.")],
        role: "Tree service owner",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell us about your tree service.", "\"I run a tree service. We cut, trim, and haul trees, and my chainsaws and generator are the tools of my business. I locked them in a trailer each night.\""), .direct("What did you find on {DATE}?", "\"I found the locked trailer cut open. Two chainsaws and a generator were gone, and the lock had been cut with bolt cutters.\""), .direct("What did the trailer camera show?", "\"A figure in a hood cutting the lock at 3:05 in the morning. The camera does not show a face, and the figure left on foot.\""), .direct("How did you find the saws again?", "\"Nine days later, a yard-sale post from {D}'s account showed the saws. The serial numbers on the saws matched my records.\""), .direct("What did the yard-sale post say?", "\"It listed two saws as barely used, $600 each. That is far below what they cost, and the saws had been used for years in my business.\""), .direct("How much did the tools cost you?", "\"The saws and the generator cost $8,700. I lost work for weeks while I replaced them, and I had to borrow equipment from another company.\""), .cross("Could you identify the person in the hood?", "\"No. The hood covers the face, and the camera is far from the trailer. I cannot say it was {D}.\""), .cross("Does {D} resell used tools?", "\"Apparently {D} has resold used tools for years. I did not know that until after the theft, and I never dealt with {D}.\""), .cross("Did {D} have a receipt for the saws?", "\"A scrap receipt that says two saws, $1,200 cash, with no last name. I cannot say whether it is real.\""), .cross("Did a seller go to jail later?", "\"I heard a flea-market seller was arrested later with another stolen trailer's contents. I do not know if it was the same person.\""), .cross("Did {D} cooperate when deputies came?", "\"Yes. {D} showed the saws and the receipt. {D} did not hide anything, and deputies recovered the saws at the house.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} sold tools stolen from a trailer.", "A buyer who was cheated."),
        allocution: "\"I should have asked more questions.\"",
        truths: ("A text from {DL} the day before: 'got a load of saws cheap, no questions.'", "The flea-market seller was arrested later with another stolen trailer's contents."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell the jury about how you buy and sell used tools.", "\"I buy used tools at flea markets and yard sales and resell them. I have done it for years, and I like finding good deals.\""), .direct("Where did you buy the saws?", "\"At a flea market, from a seller I did not know well. I paid $1,200 for both saws, and the seller wrote a scrap receipt.\""), .direct("Why did you list them for $600 each?", "\"That is what I thought a fair resale price was. I did not know they were stolen, and I would not have bought them if I had.\""), .direct("What did you tell the deputies?", "\"I told them where I bought the saws and showed them the receipt. I gave the saws back and told them everything I knew.\""), .direct("What do you know about the person who sold them to you?", "\"Only a first name and a stall at the market. I did not ask for more. I know now I should have asked for a last name.\""), .direct("Looking back, how do you feel about what happened?", "\"I am cheated and ashamed. I lost money, and I caused a business owner to lose tools. I am sorry to the owner.\""), .cross("You texted a friend the day before about a load of saws cheap, no questions, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I wrote that. It was a poor choice of words, and I know it sounds like I did not care where they came from.\""), .cross("You paid $1,200 for tools worth much more, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It was cheap. I took it for a bargain, and I know a bargain that big should have raised my suspicion.\""), .cross("The receipt has no last name, does it?", "\"No. It says two saws, $1,200 cash, and nothing more. I did not ask for a better receipt.\""), .cross("You posted the saws for sale only nine days later, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I wanted to sell them quickly. I did not know about the theft, and I did not think the timing mattered.\""), .cross("The serial numbers match the owner's records, don't they?", "\"Yes. I did not check them when I bought the saws. I understand why the jury may think I should have checked.\"")],
        openings: ("On {DATE}, {V} found a locked trailer cut open, and two chainsaws and a generator were gone. Nine days later a yard-sale post from {D}'s account listed the saws, and the serial numbers matched {V}'s.", "The defense will present a buyer and reseller of used tools who bought the saws at a flea market for $1,200 and did not know they were stolen. A cheap buy is not a theft."),
        closings: ("A cut lock, a hooded figure at 3:05, matching serial numbers, and a yard-sale post with a text the day before that said a load of saws cheap, no questions. The saws came to {D}.", "A flea-market buy, a scrap receipt, and a seller who was later arrested with another stolen trailer's contents. The State has not proved that {D} took the saws from the trailer."),
        timeline: [(-1, "{DL} texts about cheap saws."), (0, "3:05 a.m.: the lock is cut."), (9, "The yard-sale post."), (10, "Deputies recover the saws.")],
        identified: "A yard-sale post and serial numbers.",
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "searchSeizure"])

    static let odometerRollbackV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.odometerRollback",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Dealer Sold Pickup With 92,000 Miles Missing, Records Show", "Oil Change Receipt Gives Away Rolled-Back Truck"],
        law: "falsePretenses",
        threshold: 10,
        spec: "Obtained $24,500 from {V} by selling a 2018 pickup truck with an odometer rolled back from 151,000 miles to 59,000, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 42...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, {V} took a pickup bought four months earlier from {D}'s lot for a service. The mechanic pulled a prior oil-change record showing 144,000 miles. The odometer read 61,000. {DL} says the truck was bought as-is from an auction and was never altered by {D.him}.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Service Records", "An oil change at 144,000 miles one year earlier."), E(.digital, 3, "Module Readout", "Engine computer records 151,000 miles."), E(.physical, 2, "Programmer", "A handheld mileage programmer in the lot office.", .search), E(.document, 2, "Signed Disclosure", "{D} certifies 59,000 miles as actual.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "As-Is Contract", "{V} signed a no-warranty contract."), E(.statement, 1, "Auction Sheet", "{DL} says the auction sheet listed 'mileage exempt.'")],
        role: "Mechanic",
        exam: [.direct("Walk the jury through your work as a mechanic.", "\"I repair trucks and cars. I read service records, check odometers against computer modules, and I often see mileage that does not add up.\""), .direct("What did {V} bring in on {DATE}?", "\"A pickup bought four months earlier from {D}'s lot. {V} wanted a service, and I pulled the prior records on the truck.\""), .direct("What did you find in the service records?", "\"A prior oil-change record showing 144,000 miles about a year earlier. The odometer read only 61,000 when it was in my shop.\""), .direct("What did the engine computer show?", "\"The module recorded 151,000 miles. That is about ninety thousand more than the dashboard showed, and the module is harder to alter.\""), .direct("What did {D} certify on the disclosure?", "\"A signed disclosure certifying 59,000 miles as actual. That is the number {V} relied on when buying the truck.\""), .direct("What did you tell {V}?", "\"That the odometer had been rolled back. I showed {V} the oil-change record and the computer's reading, and {V} called deputies.\""), .cross("Did {V} sign an as-is contract?", "\"Yes. {V} signed a no-warranty contract. But an as-is sale does not excuse a false mileage disclosure.\""), .cross("Can you say who altered the odometer?", "\"No. I can only say it was altered. I do not know who did it, or when it happened.\""), .cross("Did the previous owner admit rolling it back?", "\"I understand the previous owner admitted rolling it back before the auction. I did not speak with the previous owner myself.\""), .cross("Did {D} know the truck had been altered?", "\"I cannot say. {D} says the truck was bought as-is from an auction. I only know what the records show.\""), .cross("Was a mileage programmer used on the truck?", "\"The programmer's log shows a session the day before the sale. That is a tool used for repairs, and it can also be used to change mileage.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Auction clerk",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Please tell us about your job at the auction.", "\"I am a clerk at a vehicle auction. I handle auction sheets, titles, and mileage notes, and I see hundreds of trucks each month.\""), .direct("Does an auction sheet sometimes list mileage exempt?", "\"Yes. Mileage exempt is used for vehicles over a certain age. The sheet means the mileage is not guaranteed, and buyers know that.\""), .direct("Do auctions check mileage on every truck?", "\"No. We rely on the seller's statement. We do not read the computer module on every truck, and many trucks have never been tested.\""), .direct("How do dealers handle that kind of sheet?", "\"Many dealers check the odometer against records themselves. Some do not, and some trust the sheet as it reads.\""), .direct("What do you know about {D}'s purchase of the truck?", "\"{D} bought the truck at our auction, as-is. The sheet listed it as mileage exempt, and nothing at the auction suggested it had been altered.\""), .direct("Have you seen odometer rollbacks at your auction?", "\"Occasionally. They are hard to catch, because sellers can alter the dash without anyone at the auction knowing.\""), .cross("Did the sheet say mileage exempt for this truck?", "\"For older trucks, yes. This truck was a 2018, so the exemption would not apply under the rule, and I do not know why the sheet listed it.\""), .cross("Did you check the mileage on that truck?", "\"No. We do not check every truck. I only know what the paperwork said when it came through.\""), .cross("Did the seller of the truck tell you about the rollback?", "\"No. The seller said nothing about it. I learned about it afterward when the deputies called.\""), .cross("Could {D} have caught the rollback?", "\"Possibly. A careful dealer might have read the module. I cannot say that {D} should have done that, but it would have helped.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever ask you about the mileage?", "\"No. {D} did not ask me about it. I was not asked about the mileage until after the sale was reported.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} rolled back an odometer and sold the truck.", "An as-is sale of an altered truck."),
        allocution: "\"I took advantage of someone who trusted me, and I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The mileage programmer's log shows a session the day before the sale.", "The previous owner admitted rolling it back before the auction."),
        defendant: [.direct("Describe your lot for the jury.", "\"I run a used car lot. I buy trucks at auction, check them over, and resell them. Most of my customers are local, and I try to be fair.\""), .direct("Did you alter the truck?", "\"No. I did not touch the odometer. I bought the truck at auction and sold it as I received it.\""), .direct("What did you tell {V} about the mileage?", "\"I told {V} what the odometer said. I signed the disclosure with the mileage listed. I did not know it was wrong.\""), .direct("What was on the auction sheet?", "\"The sheet listed mileage exempt. I took that to mean the mileage was not verified, and I did not question it.\""), .direct("Why was a programmer used on the truck the day before the sale?", "\"It was used for a repair. A technician plugged it in to fix a sensor. I did not use it on the odometer.\""), .direct("What did you do when {V} said the mileage was wrong?", "\"I offered to look into it. I told {V} I did not know about it, and I said I would call the auction.\""), .cross("You signed a disclosure of 59,000 miles, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I signed what I was given. I did not verify it against the computer, and I know I should have done more.\""), .cross("A programmer was used the day before you sold the truck, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. A technician used it for a repair, and I did not watch. I understand how that looks, but I did not use it to alter the mileage.\""), .cross("The truck's engine computer says 151,000 miles, doesn't it?", "\"That is what the mechanic says. I never read the module, and I would not have sold it as 59,000 if I had known.\""), .cross("You buy and sell many trucks, don't you?", "\"Yes. I have done it for years. I check as much as I can, but I cannot read every module on every truck.\""), .cross("The previous owner admitted rolling back the odometer, didn't the previous owner?", "\"I heard that later. I did not know it then. I feel cheated too, and I did not know the mileage was false.\"")],
        openings: ("On {DATE}, a mechanic pulled a prior oil-change record showing 144,000 miles on a pickup {V} bought from {D}'s lot, while the odometer read 61,000. The engine computer recorded 151,000 miles.", "The defense will present an as-is auction truck, a sheet that listed mileage exempt, and a dealer who did not alter anything. An as-is sale of an altered truck is not a fraud by the dealer."),
        closings: ("An oil change at 144,000 miles, a module that reads 151,000, an odometer at 61,000, and a signed disclosure of 59,000. A programmer session the day before the sale shows who had the tools.", "A truck bought as-is at auction, a previous owner who admitted rolling it back, and a dealer who signed what the auction paperwork said. The State has not proved that {D} altered anything."),
        timeline: [(-370, "An oil change records 144,000 miles."), (-120, "The truck is sold to {V}."), (0, "The mechanic finds the record."), (3, "{V} calls deputies.")],
        identified: "A prior service record.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let ballgamePistolV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.ballgamePistol",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Pistol Falls From Bag at Softball Tournament, Official Calls Deputy", "Out-of-State Permit Not Honored in North Carolina"],
        law: "concealedWeapon",
        spec: "Carried a concealed pistol on or about {D.his} person, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 21...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A loaded pistol fell from a waist bag as {D} took out a glove at a softball tournament on {DATE}. A tournament official called a deputy. {D} showed a permit from another state. {DL} says {D.he} believed it was honored here.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Pistol", "A loaded pistol in a waist bag.", .search), E(.document, 2, "Permit Card", "A permit issued by another state that North Carolina does not honor.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Reciprocity Site", "{DL} says a website listed North Carolina as honored.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role?", "\"I am a sheriff's deputy. I responded to the softball tournament.\""), .direct("What happened on {DATE}?", "\"A loaded pistol fell from a waist bag as {D} took out a glove.\""), .direct("Who called you?", "\"A tournament official who saw the pistol drop.\""), .direct("What did {DL} show you?", "\"A permit from another state.\""), .direct("Does North Carolina honor it?", "\"No. That permit is not honored here.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"That a website listed North Carolina as honored.\""), .direct("What did the tournament official tell you when you arrived at the softball tournament?", "\"The official said a loaded pistol had fallen from a waist bag when {D} took out a glove. I found {D} with the pistol and a permit from another state.\""), .direct("What did you do with the pistol and the permit after you took them?", "\"I secured the pistol, photographed the permit, and read it carefully. It was issued by another state, and North Carolina does not honor it, so I wrote up a charge for carrying concealed.\""), .cross("Did {DL} try to hide the pistol?", "\"No. It fell out by accident, and {D} cooperated right away.\""), .cross("Was the pistol registered?", "\"It belonged to {D}. I found no theft report.\""), .cross("Did {DL} have a valid permit anywhere?", "\"Yes, in the home state. Just not one honored here.\""), .cross("Was anyone threatened?", "\"No. Nobody was threatened.\""), .cross("Did {DL} tell you about the website?", "\"Yes. {D} said the website listed this state as honored.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} carried a concealed pistol without a valid permit.", "A mistake about reciprocity."),
        allocution: "\"I should have checked. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("A friend had warned {DL} before the trip that the permit was not honored here.", "The reciprocity page {DL} used was out of date."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why do you carry a pistol?", "\"I always carry for protection. I hold a permit from my home state and take that responsibility seriously.\""), .direct("Did you know the permit was not honored here?", "\"I checked a reciprocity website before the trip and it listed this state as honored. I trusted it.\""), .direct("Did anyone warn you about it?", "\"A friend mentioned it might not be honored. I did not take it seriously enough and I regret that.\""), .direct("Why was the page wrong?", "\"It was out of date. I never looked at the date at the bottom, and That is on me.\""), .direct("How did the pistol come to fall out?", "\"I reached into the waist bag for a glove and it slipped out. I had forgotten it was in there.\""), .direct("Looking back, how do you feel about it?", "\"Foolish and embarrassed. I should have double-checked with the state itself.\""), .direct("What did the friend who warned you say about the permit?", "\"A friend told me before the trip that the permit was not honored in North Carolina. I checked an old website instead, and I trusted the website.\""), .cross("Your permit is not valid in this state, is it?", "\"I know that now. It was not honored here.\""), .cross("A friend warned you before the trip, didn't they?", "\"Yes. I did not follow up as I own that.\""), .cross("The pistol was loaded, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I carry it loaded.\""), .cross("You brought it to a softball tournament where children play, didn't you?", "\"Yes, and that makes it worse.\""), .cross("The website you used had a date you did not check, didn't it?", "\"Yes. It was my mistake.\"")],
        openings: ("A loaded pistol fell from a waist bag as {D} took out a glove at a softball tournament, and a tournament official called a deputy. {D} showed a permit from another state that North Carolina does not honor.", "A website listed North Carolina as honored, and {D} trusted it. {D} says the page was out of date, and the State must prove that {D} knew the permit was not valid here."),
        closings: ("A loaded pistol, a permit that North Carolina does not honor, and a friend who warned {D} before the trip. {D} carried a concealed pistol without a valid permit.", "A mistake about reciprocity based on a page that was out of date. The State has not proved that {D} knew the permit was not honored in North Carolina."),
        timeline: [(-3, "{DL} reads a reciprocity page."), (0, "A pistol falls from the bag."), (0, "A deputy arrives."), (0, "The deputy takes the pistol.")],
        identified: "A tournament official and a deputy.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "mistakeOfFact"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let schoolZoneCrashV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.schoolZoneCrash",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Driver Hits Parent Volunteer Directing Dismissal Line", "Cold Medicine or Something Stronger?"],
        law: "felonyDBV",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Operated a motor vehicle in a school zone while impaired, causing serious injury to {V}, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 20...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, {D} drove around stopped cars at an elementary school dismissal line and hit {V}, a parent volunteer holding a stop sign. {D} blew .10 an hour later. {DL} says {D.he} was feverish and took cold medicine.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Blood Test", "0.10 about an hour after the crash."), E(.video, 2, "School Camera", "A car drives onto the shoulder at about 35 mph in the zone."), E(.video, 2, "Body Camera", "{D} speaks slowly and sways.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Cold Medicine", "{DL} says {D.he} took cold medicine.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("Please explain your role as a sheriff's deputy.", "\"I patrol the county and investigate crashes. I handle impaired driving cases, take blood samples, and review cameras after a crash near a school.\""), .direct("What did you see on the school camera?", "\"A car driving onto the shoulder around the dismissal line at about 35 miles an hour in a 15 mile zone. The car struck {V}.\""), .direct("Who was {V}?", "\"{V} was a parent volunteer holding a stop sign at the dismissal line. {V} was hit while directing cars, and {V} was taken to the hospital.\""), .direct("What did you observe about {D} at the stop?", "\"{D} was flushed and spoke slowly, and swayed on the shoulder. My body camera shows {D}'s speech and balance clearly.\""), .direct("What did the blood test show?", "\"A blood alcohol level of 0.10 about an hour after the crash. Blood was drawn at 4:15 p.m., and the crash happened at about 3:10.\""), .direct("What did you find in {D}'s car?", "\"A bottle of cold medicine. An empty pint bottle was under the passenger seat, and I photographed both for the report.\""), .cross("Was {D} feverish?", "\"{D} looked flushed. That could mean fever or alcohol. I did not take {D}'s temperature, and I cannot say which.\""), .cross("Did a coworker say {D} took cold medicine?", "\"Yes. A coworker confirms {D} left work feverish and took two doses of cold medicine. I did not speak with the coworker myself.\""), .cross("Whose bottle was the pint bottle?", "\"I cannot say. {D} says it was not {D}'s. It was empty, and I did not test it for prints.\""), .cross("Can cold medicine show alcohol on a test?", "\"Some syrups contain a little alcohol. But I do not think that would produce a 0.10, and I am not a toxicologist.\""), .cross("Did {D} try to leave the scene?", "\"No. {D} stayed at the scene and cooperated. {D} said {D} did not see the dismissal line until it was too late.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Toxicologist",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What do you do as a toxicologist?", "\"I analyze blood and other samples for alcohol and drugs. I testify about how different substances affect the body and how they show up in tests.\""), .direct("Can cold syrup show alcohol on a blood test?", "\"A little, in some syrups. But the level would be much lower than 0.10, and one or two doses would not reach that.\""), .direct("What could explain a reading of 0.10?", "\"Drinking is the most likely cause. Other factors can raise or lower a reading, but a 0.10 usually means a person had several drinks.\""), .direct("What does the timing of the blood draw tell us?", "\"The blood was drawn about an hour after the crash. Alcohol levels can still be rising or falling, and that affects what the number meant at the time of driving.\""), .direct("How do fever and cold medicine affect a driver?", "\"They can cause drowsiness and dizziness. Those effects can slow reaction time and make it harder to judge a scene, even without alcohol.\""), .direct("What would you need to see to say cold medicine caused a 0.10?", "\"I would need to know the exact product and dose. A typical syrup does not carry enough alcohol, so I doubt it.\""), .cross("Can syrup show alcohol?", "\"A little. It would not reach 0.10 with ordinary doses. I told the jury that, and I am not offering it as an explanation.\""), .cross("What else could explain it?", "\"Drinking. That is the usual explanation for a 0.10, and I cannot rule it out from the number alone.\""), .cross("Did you test {D}'s blood yourself?", "\"No. I reviewed the lab's results. I did not collect the sample, and I cannot say how it was handled.\""), .cross("Would a pint bottle under the seat change your opinion?", "\"It could suggest drinking. I cannot say who drank from it, and I did not test it, but it is relevant.\""), .cross("Could {D} have been impaired by cold medicine alone?", "\"Possibly, by drowsiness. But that would not produce a 0.10, and the blood test is separate from the effects of the medicine.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drove drunk around a dismissal line.", "Cold medicine and a fever."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. I hope you walk again.\"",
