        defendant: [.direct("What can you tell us about your time as a vendor at the market?", "\"I sold produce at the market for years. I got along with most vendors, and I felt the market was part of my life.\""), .direct("Why were you dropped from the market?", "\"I was told I broke a stall rule. I disagreed, and I was angry. I did not think it was fair, but I accepted it.\""), .direct("Whose cap was found at the scene?", "\"Mine, from months ago. I left it at the market when I was dropped, and a rival vendor wore one like it.\""), .direct("Did you rob {V}?", "\"No. I did not. I was not in the lot that evening, and I never pushed anyone or took any bag.\""), .direct("Where did the $2,000 deposit come from?", "\"From a motorcycle I sold that week. I had advertised it for a while, and I have the sale record to show it.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"The word for it is hurt. I have never hurt anyone, and I do not understand why my cap ended up at the scene.\""), .cross("You deposited $2,000 in cash two days later, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It came from selling my motorcycle. I know the timing looks bad, but it is the truth.\""), .cross("You were angry about being dropped from the market, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I was angry. I did not plan to rob anyone, and being angry does not make me a robber.\""), .cross("The cap carried your DNA, didn't it?", "\"Yes. It was my cap. I wore it for years, and I left it at the market when I was dropped.\""), .cross("A van matching yours was seen leaving the lot, wasn't it?", "\"That is what I am told. I own a common van. I was not in the lot, and I did not drive away from there.\""), .cross("You do not have an alibi for 5:40 that evening, do you?", "\"I was at home, alone. I did not think I needed an alibi, and I know that is a weakness in my case.\"")],
        openings: ("As the treasurer of a farmers market carried $7,400 in cash to a car after closing, someone in a rain jacket shoved {V} down and took the bag. A ball cap was left behind, and DNA matched {D}, a vendor dropped from the market.", "The defense will present a cap left at the market long before the robbery, a rival vendor who wore a similar one, and a motorcycle sale that explains a $2,000 deposit. A cap is not a robber."),
        closings: ("A shove, a stolen bag with $7,400, a cap with {D}'s DNA, and a cash deposit two days later. {D} was angry about being dropped from the market, and the cap was left at the scene.", "An old cap left at the market, a similar cap worn by a rival vendor, and a motorcycle sale. The State has not proved that {D} was the figure in the rain jacket."),
        timeline: [(-50, "{DL} is dropped from the market."), (0, "5:40 p.m.: the shove."), (0, "5:45 p.m.: {V} calls deputies."), (2, "A cash deposit.")],
        identified: "DNA on a ball cap.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "I cannot walk to my car alone.")

    static let nursingHomeNeglectV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.nursingHomeNeglect",
        category: .family,
        headlines: ["Memory Care Resident Found Frozen Outside After Door Alarm Was Disabled", "Administrator Charged; Alarm Off for Eleven Days"],
        law: "invManslaughter",
