        summary: "On {DATE}, {V}, 84, a memory care resident, wandered out an exit at night and was found frozen 200 yards away. The door alarm had been disabled for eleven days under {D}'s code. One aide covered 38 residents. {DL}, the administrator, says the alarm kept failing and {D.he} begged the owners for repair parts.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Alarm Panel Log", "The door alarm disabled for eleven days under {D}'s admin code."), E(.document, 3, "Staffing Schedule", "One aide for 38 residents overnight."), E(.forensic, 3, "Autopsy", "Hypothermia.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 1, "Repair Requests", "{DL} emailed the owners twice for a new sensor.")],
        role: "Night nurse",
        exam: [.direct("What are your duties as a night nurse?", "\"I work the overnight shift in the memory care unit. I give medications, check on residents, and respond to alarms, often as the only nurse on the floor.\""), .direct("What happened on the night {V} left the unit?", "\"{V}, who was 84, wandered out an exit at about two in the morning. The door alarm did not sound, and {V} was found frozen 200 yards away at seven.\""), .direct("What was the status of the door alarm?", "\"It had been disabled for eleven days under {D}'s admin code. The alarm panel log shows the code used to turn it off.\""), .direct("How was the unit staffed that night?", "\"One aide covered 38 residents overnight. I was on another hall, and the aide could not watch every door while helping residents.\""), .direct("How did {V} die?", "\"The autopsy found hypothermia. {V} was outside in the cold for hours, and by the time we found {V}, nothing could be done.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell staff about the alarm?", "\"{D} texted staff to leave it off, saying {D} was tired of the beeping. I saw that text, and I did not argue with it.\""), .cross("Did the alarm ring falsely often?", "\"Yes. It rang many times a night. A sensor kept failing, and the beeping woke residents and exhausted staff.\""), .cross("Did {D} ask for a repair?", "\"Yes. {D} emailed the owners twice for a new sensor. The regional manager refused the repair order twice, in an email {D} forwarded to staff.\""), .cross("Was {D} the only person who could disable the alarm?", "\"No. Other staff had codes as well. But the log shows {D}'s admin code was used, and I cannot say who pressed the button.\""), .cross("Did you ever tell {D} the alarm was needed?", "\"I told {D} I was worried about residents who wander. {D} said the owners had refused the sensor, and I let it go.\""), .cross("Could the staffing have been different?", "\"The owners set the staffing. One aide for 38 residents is below what I think is safe, and I told {D} so more than once.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Maintenance supervisor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Please tell us about your work as maintenance supervisor.", "\"I maintain the building, including doors, alarms, and sensors. I replace parts when owners approve them, and I fix what I can on my own.\""), .direct("Why was the alarm off?", "\"A bad sensor kept setting it off. It rang over and over each night, and I could not fix it without a replacement part.\""), .direct("What did you ask {D} about the repair?", "\"I told {D} I needed a new sensor. {D} told me {D} had asked the owners, and the owners refused the repair twice.\""), .direct("Who asked you to leave the alarm off?", "\"{D} did. I said it was a bad idea, but {D} said the beeping was keeping residents awake. I did not want to push back.\""), .direct("What would a new sensor have cost?", "\"Not much. A few hundred dollars. I could have installed it in an hour, and I wish the owners had approved it.\""), .direct("What did you see on the night {V} left?", "\"I was not there. I came in the next morning after the call. I saw the door and the alarm panel, and I felt sick.\""), .cross("Did you tell anyone the alarm was dangerous to leave off?", "\"I told {D}. I did not tell the state. I knew residents could wander, and I should have pushed harder.\""), .cross("Did you have the authority to replace the sensor?", "\"No. I needed approval from the owners. I could have bought it myself, but I would not have been reimbursed.\""), .cross("Did you check the door each day?", "\"Yes, but only for damage. I did not check whether the alarm was enabled, and I assumed someone was watching it.\""), .cross("Did {D} take any steps to protect residents while the alarm was off?", "\"I did not see any. I did not see a guard or a schedule for checking the door, and I did not ask.\""), .cross("Did you remind {D} that the alarm had been off for days?", "\"Once. I mentioned it near the end of the week. {D} said the owners were working on it, and I let it go.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} disabled a door alarm and left residents unprotected.", "A failing sensor and owners who ignored requests."),
        allocution: "\"I'll carry this the rest of my life.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} texted staff 'leave it off, I'm tired of the beeping.'", "The owners' regional manager refused the sensor repair order twice, in an email {DL} forwarded."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell us about your job as administrator.", "\"I run the nursing home day to day. I manage staff, budgets, and safety, and I report to owners who decide what money we can spend.\""), .direct("Why did you disable the door alarm?", "\"The sensor kept failing. It rang all night and woke residents. I silenced it because staff and residents could not sleep, and I told the owners.\""), .direct("What did you ask the owners to do?", "\"I emailed them twice for a new sensor. The regional manager refused the repair twice, and I forwarded those emails to staff.\""), .direct("What did you tell staff about the alarm?", "\"I texted staff to leave it off because I was tired of the beeping. I should have told them to watch the door instead.\""), .direct("Did you post a guard at the door?", "\"No. I should have posted someone. We did not have enough staff, and I did not find a way to cover it.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"Devastated, more than anything. {V} died because of choices I made. I begged for parts, and I should have done more to protect residents.\""), .cross("The alarm was off for eleven days, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I know how long it was off. I thought a failing sensor was worse than no alarm, and I was wrong.\""), .cross("One aide covered 38 residents, didn't the schedule say so?", "\"One aide covered 38 residents overnight. The owners set that staffing, but I approved the schedule and I know it was too thin.\""), .cross("You texted staff to leave it off, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I wrote that I was tired of the beeping. It was a thoughtless message, and I regret it deeply.\""), .cross("You never reported the alarm shutdown to the state, did you?", "\"No. I did not. I thought I could fix it with the owners first, and I did not realize it was dangerous.\""), .cross("You could have posted a staff member at the door, couldn't you?", "\"Yes. I could have asked someone to stay. I did not, and I know that decision matters.\"")],
        openings: ("On {DATE}, {V}, 84, a memory care resident, wandered out an exit at night and was found frozen 200 yards away. The door alarm had been disabled for eleven days under {D}'s code, and one aide covered 38 residents.", "The defense will present a failing sensor, two written requests for repair, and owners who refused the order twice. {D} begged for parts, and the State must prove {D} acted with knowing disregard."),
        closings: ("An alarm off for eleven days under {D}'s own code, a text that said leave it off, one aide for 38 residents, and an 84-year-old who froze 200 yards from the door.", "A broken sensor, two emails begging for repairs, and owners who refused them twice. {D} did not choose to leave residents unprotected, and the State has not proved otherwise."),
        timeline: [(-11, "The alarm is disabled."), (-8, "{DL} emails the owners."), (0, "2 a.m.: {V} leaves the unit."), (0, "7 a.m.: {V} is found.")],
        identified: "An alarm panel log.",
        aggravating: ["The victim was elderly and dependent on the defendant's facility"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "{V} knew every nurse's name.",
        genders: ["D": .female, "V": .female])

    static let fakeAccountsV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.fakeAccounts",
        category: .cyber,
        headlines: ["Anonymous Emails to Client List Followed Job Promotion", "Spelling Slip Ties Seven Addresses Together"],
