        defense: [E(.document, 1, "Mental Health Records", "{DL} had been treated for episodes of confusion.")],
        role: "SBI agent",
        exam: [.direct("Tell us about your work as an SBI agent.", "\"I investigate major crimes for the State Bureau of Investigation. I collect video, vehicle data, messages, and records, and I interview witnesses and the people charged.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the day of the county fair?", "\"On {DATE}, a pickup truck was driven past a gate and across a crowded midway for about 200 feet. Two people died, including {V}, and thirty were hurt.\""), .direct("What did the vehicle data show?", "\"The accelerator was fully pressed for eight seconds with no braking. The camera shows the pickup accelerating through the midway without slowing.\""), .direct("What did {D} text that day?", "\"At noon, {D} texted a former partner that tonight you will know what I am. That message was sent hours before the pickup entered the midway.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell a friend that morning?", "\"{D} told a friend that tonight everyone will remember my name. The friend gave that statement to us after the fair.\""), .direct("How was {D} arrested?", "\"{D} was arrested walking out of the fairgrounds at about 8:10. {D} did not flee in the pickup, and {D} was arrested without a struggle.\""), .cross("Did {D} have mental health treatment before?", "\"Yes. Records say {D} had been treated for episodes of confusion. I do not know how much that affected the day of the fair.\""), .cross("Was {D} on medication that changed before the fair?", "\"The records show that {D}'s medication was doubled by a pharmacy error two days before. I do not know what effect that had.\""), .cross("Did {D} try to hide after the incident?", "\"No. {D} walked out of the fairgrounds and was arrested. {D} was calm, and I did not see an attempt to flee.\""), .cross("Did {D} explain why {D} drove into the midway?", "\"{D} said {D} was confused and sick. {D} did not remember pressing the accelerator for eight seconds.\""), .cross("Did you find any plan written down?", "\"No. We found the texts and the statement to a friend. We did not find a written plan or a list of targets.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Psychiatrist",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Describe your work as a psychiatrist.", "\"I treat patients with severe mental illness. I evaluate their medication, their thinking, and whether they could understand what they were doing at a particular time.\""), .direct("What did you learn about {D}'s history?", "\"{D} had been treated for episodes of confusion. The records show a history of delusional thinking and gaps in memory under stress.\""), .direct("How can a medication error affect a person like {D}?", "\"Doubling a dose can cause severe confusion, agitation, and loss of memory. It can make a person act without understanding what they are doing.\""), .direct("What did you conclude about {D}'s state of mind that day?", "\"I believe {D} was in a mental crisis. {D} was confused, sick, and may not have understood the consequences of the act.\""), .direct("What would an eight-second acceleration suggest to you?", "\"It could suggest a loss of control. A person acting deliberately would often brake or turn, and {D} did not do either.\""), .direct("What did you see when you evaluated {D}?", "\"I saw a person who could not recall much of the day. {D} was horrified when told what happened, and {D} was in shock.\""), .cross("Could {D} have been confused?", "\"It is possible. The records and the pharmacy error support that. I cannot say with certainty how much.\""), .cross("Did {D} drive past a gate?", "\"Yes. The camera shows the pickup going past a gate. I do not know whether {D} understood that at the time.\""), .cross("Did {D} send a threat that noon?", "\"Yes. The text is on the record. I cannot say what {D} meant by it, and it could be consistent with anger or with confusion.\""), .cross("Did {D} tell a friend that morning that everyone would remember {D}'s name?", "\"The friend says so. That statement could suggest a plan, and I cannot rule that out from the records.\""), .cross("Does mental illness excuse what happened?", "\"Not by itself. The law has its own test. I can only describe what I found about {D}'s condition.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} deliberately drove into a crowd.", "A mind in crisis."),
