        role: "Fundraiser manager",
        exam: [.direct("What did you learn on {DATE}?", "\"The down payment for a new engine could not be made.\""), .direct("What did the dinner tallies show?", "\"$142,000 raised over four years.\""), .direct("What did the account hold?", "\"$81,000.\""), .direct("Who made the deposits?", "\"{D}, alone, as auxiliary treasurer.\""), .direct("What did the personal account show?", "\"Cash deposits after each dinner.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"That cash paid for supplies, unrecorded.\""), .direct("What did the bank records show about deposits compared with the dinner tallies?", "\"The tallies counted $142,000 raised over four years, but the bank records show only $81,000 deposited. {D} made every deposit alone, so no one else could account for the difference.\""), .direct("What did the fire chief tell you about the engine approval and the deadline?", "\"The new engine had been approved, and the down payment was due. When the check bounced, the department could not make the purchase, and the chief had to tell the council.\""), .direct("How were the dinner funds supposed to be tracked by the auxiliary?", "\"Cash taken at the door was supposed to be counted by two people and deposited the next day. Here, {D} counted and deposited alone for four years, without any second signature.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} take any money?", "\"No. I traced bank records and deposits.\""), .cross("Were the dinner tallies reliable?", "\"They were handwritten. An old flood took earlier books, so some are weak.\""), .cross("How much did {DL} deposit into a personal account?", "\"Cash after each dinner, in amounts that add up to a large sum.\""), .cross("Did {DL} cooperate?", "\"Yes. {D} answered questions without delay.\""), .cross("Did the auxiliary have a second signer?", "\"No. {D} made every deposit alone.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Auxiliary volunteer",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What is your role with the auxiliary?", "\"I am a volunteer. I help set up the dinners and clean up afterward.\""), .direct("How were the dinners run?", "\"Informally. We took cash at the door, and {D} counted it in the back at the end.\""), .direct("Were the tallies always accurate?", "\"Not always. Counting was rushed and the handwriting was messy.\""), .direct("What happened to the old books?", "\"A basement flood ruined them. We lost years of records.\""), .direct("How would you describe {DL}?", "\"Dedicated. {D} put in long hours and I never saw a sign of dishonesty.\""), .direct("Did you see {DL} spend on supplies?", "\"Yes. I saw {D} come back with grocery bags and paper goods many times.\""), .direct("What did you see about how the dinner cash was handled at the door?", "\"We took cash at the door and counted it at the end of the night. {D} counted and took the bag home to deposit, and no one else watched the count.\""), .direct("Did anyone ever check the tallies against the deposits during those four years?", "\"Not that I know of. We trusted the numbers {D} gave us at the meetings, and nobody asked for the bank statements until the engine purchase came up.\""), .direct("What was the mood in the auxiliary when the shortfall was discovered?", "\"Shock. Everyone had worked hard for years on those dinners, and we could not understand how the account held so much less than the tallies had counted.\""), .cross("Did you keep receipts for what {DL} bought?", "\"No. We never did.\""), .cross("Who counted the cash at the end of dinners?", "\"{D}, mostly alone.\""), .cross("Did anyone check the counts?", "\"No. We trusted {D}.\""), .cross("Did {DL} ever tell you about repaying personal money?", "\"Not to me.\""), .cross("Did any other volunteer make deposits?", "\"No. Only {D}.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} kept dinner money for personal use.", "Unrecorded supplies and sloppy books."),
        allocution: "\"I borrowed it and could not repay. I am sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} paid off a boat loan the same spring.", "The auxiliary's old books were lost in a basement flood, so the tallies were unreliable."),
        defendant: [.direct("What was your role in the auxiliary?", "\"I was the treasurer. I counted the cash after the dinners and made the deposits.\""), .direct("Where did the missing money go?", "\"Supplies for the dinners: food, plates, decorations, and equipment. I paid in cash and did not keep every receipt.\""), .direct("Why were those purchases unrecorded?", "\"The books were informal, and the old ones were lost in a basement flood. I should have kept better records.\""), .direct("What about the cash deposits to your own account?", "\"I thought I was repaying myself for things I had bought for the dinners. I did not think of it as stealing.\""), .direct("What about the boat loan you paid off?", "\"That was from savings and a bonus. The timing was a coincidence.\""), .direct("How are you coping with what happened?", "\"Ashamed. The department needed it and I let people down.\""), .direct("What did you do with the cash that never reached the bank?", "\"Some paid for supplies that were never recorded. I also paid off a boat loan that spring, and I know that looks like I used the dinner money myself.\""), .cross("About $61,000 is missing between the tallies and the bank, isn't it?", "\"That is the gap that people say. I cannot account for all of it.\""), .cross("You deposited cash into your own account after each dinner, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I did.\""), .cross("You paid off a boat loan that same spring, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did.\""), .cross("You kept no receipts for the supplies, did you?", "\"Not for most. That was careless.\""), .cross("You made every deposit alone, correct?", "\"Yes.\"")],
        openings: ("The fire chief learned that the down payment for a new engine could not be made. Dinner tallies showed $142,000 raised over four years, but the account held only $81,000, and {D}, the auxiliary's treasurer, made every deposit alone.", "A flooded basement took the auxiliary's old books, and cash paid for supplies went unrecorded. {D} says the tallies were unreliable, and the State must prove that {D} kept the money."),
        closings: ("$142,000 counted and $81,000 deposited, every deposit made by {D} alone, and a boat loan paid off the same spring. The money raised for a fire engine did not all reach the bank.", "Old books lost in a basement flood and supplies paid in cash without a record. The State has not proved that {D} kept money that the tallies cannot reliably show."),
        timeline: [(-1460, "{DL} becomes treasurer."), (-60, "A new engine is approved."), (0, "The down payment bounces."), (7, "An audit begins.")],
        identified: "Tallies and bank records.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction)

